-- title:
--   From HTo G Interpolation Eligible Sandwich Total Eq Type Sum
-- statement:
--   **An interpolation-eligible sandwich total splits by exact Boolean type.**
--
--   Let `params` have a field model, let `family` be an indexed polynomial submeasurement family, let `k` be a natural number, and let `xs` be a tuple of `k` field points. The family `interpolationEligibleSandwichFamily` is the G-hat sandwich family restricted to completed-slice tuples whose support has size at least `d+1`. Its total operator is exactly
--
--   $$
--   \bigl(\operatorname{interpolationEligibleSandwichFamily}(\mathrm{params},\mathrm{family},k,xs)\bigr).\operatorname{total}
--   =
--   \sum_{\tau\in\{0,1\}^{k}}
--   \begin{cases}
--   \displaystyle\sum_{\substack{gs:\,\operatorname{gHatTupleType}(gs)=\tau}}
--   \bigl(\operatorname{gHatSandwichFamily}(\mathrm{params},\mathrm{family},k,xs)\bigr).\operatorname{outcome}(gs),
--   &d+1\le |\tau|,\\[1ex]
--   0,&d+1>|\tau|.
--   \end{cases}
--   $$
--
--   Here $|\tau|$ is `gHatTypeWeight tau`. The result is the exact-type partition of the eligible total used by `fromHToG_averagedEligibleSandwich_total_eq_type_sum`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToG_interpolationEligibleSandwich_total_eq_type_sum`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
